godot/pull/110013#issuecomment-3302291715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110013","id":3302291715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7E1PkD","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-17T10:11:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-17T10:11:46Z","body":"> How to correctly handle udev and dbus on Linux? SOWARP_ENABLED is not present on 3.x but there is a libudev-so_wrap. Is a libdbus-so_wrap required to make it work if dbus can't be found on the system? Do we need a thirdparty/linuxbsd_headers as well? I'm a bit out of my depth with understanding how and when which libraries is used from where.\n\nOh, sorry, I didn't notice the question here 😅 If SOWRAP_ENABLED is not present in 3.x and theres libudev-so_wrap, so I assume that Godot uses sowrap here and it's not optional, so I think it's fair to only use the code parts for SOWRAP_ENABLED. SDL also uses dynamic loading of dbus and udev functions (for udev the file has to be specified in the SDL build config file, otherwise it will try to get the functions from the built game/Godot binary, but still), basically 